# SDDRA Evolution Plan: L0 to L5

Purpose:
  Define the SDDRA system maturity levels from L0 (initial) to L5 (optimized).
  Each level builds on the previous one. The system is designed to evolve
  through these levels without breaking changes.

## Maturity Levels

### L0: Initial (MVP)

Goal: Basic system works end-to-end

Characteristics:
  - Manual .sdd/ file creation
  - Simple chain execution (P1->D1->S1->C1)
  - No automation
  - No resilience patterns
  - Basic documentation

Capabilities:
  - Create .sdd/ files manually
  - Execute simple chains
  - Generate basic docs
  - Generate basic code

Limitations:
  - No skill execution model
  - No resilience
  - No automation
  - No optimization
  - No monitoring

Files:
  - PROJECT.sdd
  - INDEX.sdd
  - protocol/ROOT.sdd
  - chains/graph.sdd
  - templates/ (basic)
  - project/ (basic)

### L1: Managed

Goal: Repeatable process with basic structure

Characteristics:
  - Template-based .sdd/ generation
  - Standardized chain execution
  - Basic skill definitions
  - Manual human gates
  - Basic documentation

Capabilities:
  - Generate .sdd/ from templates
  - Execute standard chains
  - Define basic skills
  - Human approval gates
  - Token tracking

Limitations:
  - No skill execution
  - No resilience
  - No optimization
  - No self-healing
  - Limited automation

Files:
  - All L0 files
  - templates/ (expanded)
  - skills/ (basic L1-L2)
  - commands/ (basic)
  - workflow/ (basic)

### L2: Defined

Goal: Documented and standardized

Characteristics:
  - Documented processes
  - Defined skill execution model
  - Basic resilience patterns
  - Semantic versioning
  - Comprehensive documentation

Capabilities:
  - Execute skills autonomously (L1-L2)
  - Circuit breaker for failures
  - Basic checkpoint/restore
  - Semantic commits
  - Git workflow
  - Health checks

Limitations:
  - No advanced resilience
  - No intelligent automation
  - No self-healing
  - No predictive features
  - Limited optimization

Files:
  - All L1 files
  - skills/SKILL-EXECUTION.sdd
  - patterns/circuit-breaker.sdd
  - commands/sdd-health.sdd
  - .git/hooks/commit-msg
  - GIT-WORKFLOW.sdd

### L3: Quantified

Goal: Measured and optimized

Characteristics:
  - Metrics and monitoring
  - Token optimization
  - Performance tracking
  - Advanced resilience
  - Intelligent automation

Capabilities:
  - Token budget optimization
  - Context caching with metrics
  - Checkpoint/restore with metrics
  - Graceful degradation
  - Predictive token budgeting
  - Automated decision suggestions
  - Smart context loading

Limitations:
  - No self-healing
  - No advanced reasoning
  - No predictive maintenance
  - Limited learning

Files:
  - All L2 files
  - patterns/checkpoint-restore.sdd
  - patterns/graceful-degradation.sdd
  - context/cache.sdd (with metrics)
  - orchestrator/INDEX.sdd (includes reasoning patterns)
  - RESILIENCE.md

### L4: Optimized

Goal: Continuously improving

Characteristics:
  - Self-healing capabilities
  - Advanced reasoning patterns
  - Predictive maintenance
  - Resource registry with auto-update
  - Learning from past decisions

Capabilities:
  - Auto-detect corruption
  - Attempt self-repair
  - Escalate to human if needed
  - Learn from approvals/rejections
  - Predict dependencies
  - Pre-load resources
  - Intelligent gate management
  - Pattern matching for decisions

Limitations:
  - No autonomous architecture changes
  - No self-modification
  - Human still controls critical decisions

Files:
  - All L3 files
  - RESOURCES.sdd (with auto-update)
  - orchestrator/INDEX.sdd (includes reasoning patterns)
  - patterns/self-healing.sdd (if added)
  - patterns/intelligent-gates.sdd (if added)

### L5: Optimized (Peak)

Goal: Fully autonomous with human oversight

Characteristics:
  - Near-full autonomy for routine tasks
  - Advanced AI reasoning
  - Self-improving system
  - Minimal human intervention
  - Continuous optimization

Capabilities:
  - Autonomous skill execution (all levels)
  - Self-modifying templates (with approval)
  - Predictive architecture optimization
  - Automatic knowledge extraction
  - Continuous learning
  - Zero-touch operations for routine tasks
  - Automatic dependency resolution
  - Intelligent prioritization

Limitations:
  - Human still approves architecture changes
  - Human still approves production deployments
  - Human still controls security policies

Files:
  - All L4 files
  - patterns/autonomous-execution.sdd (if added)
  - patterns/self-improvement.sdd (if added)
  - Full automation of all routine tasks

## Evolution Path

### L0 -> L1: Foundation

Focus: Templates and basic automation

Tasks:
  - Create basic templates
  - Standardize chain execution
  - Add basic skills (L1-L2)
  - Add basic commands

Duration: 2-4 weeks

Deliverables:
  - templates/ with 10+ templates
  - skills/ with 20+ L1-L2 skills
  - commands/ with 5+ commands
  - Basic documentation

### L1 -> L2: Structure

Focus: Documentation and standards

Tasks:
  - Document all processes
  - Define skill execution model
  - Add resilience patterns
  - Add semantic commits
  - Add git workflow

Duration: 2-4 weeks

Deliverables:
  - SKILL-EXECUTION.sdd
  - patterns/ (circuit-breaker, checkpoint-restore, graceful-degradation)
  - commands/sdd-health.sdd
  - GIT-WORKFLOW.sdd
  - .git/hooks/commit-msg
  - Comprehensive documentation

### L2 -> L3: Measurement

Focus: Metrics and optimization

Tasks:
  - Add metrics collection
  - Optimize token usage
  - Add performance tracking
  - Add predictive features
  - Add intelligent automation

Duration: 4-6 weeks

Deliverables:
  - context/cache.sdd with metrics
  - Token optimization algorithms
  - Predictive token budgeting
  - Automated decision suggestions
  - Smart context loading

### L3 -> L4: Intelligence

Focus: Self-healing and learning

Tasks:
  - Add self-healing mechanisms
  - Add learning from past decisions
  - Add resource registry with auto-update
  - Add intelligent gate management
  - Add pattern matching

Duration: 6-8 weeks

Deliverables:
  - RESOURCES.sdd with auto-update
  - Self-healing patterns
  - Decision learning system
  - Intelligent gate management
  - Dependency pre-loading

### L4 -> L5: Autonomy

Focus: Near-full autonomy

Tasks:
  - Autonomous skill execution
  - Self-modifying templates (with approval)
  - Predictive architecture optimization
  - Continuous learning
  - Zero-touch operations

Duration: 8-12 weeks

Deliverables:
  - Autonomous execution engine
  - Self-improvement patterns
  - Advanced reasoning system
  - Zero-touch automation
  - Continuous optimization

