## Backward Compatibility

All evolution MUST maintain backward compatibility:
  - Old .sdd/ files must still load
  - Old prompts must still work
  - Old projects must still build
  - Deprecation warnings, not errors
  - Migration guides provided

## Migration Strategy

When moving between levels:
  1. Add new features without breaking old ones
  2. Mark old features as DEPRECATED
  3. Provide migration path
  4. Keep old version available for 6 months
  5. Notify users of changes

## Success Metrics

- System uptime (chains completed / attempted)
- Mean time to recovery (MTTR)
- Token efficiency
- Cache hit rate
- Decision accuracy
- Failure rate per stage
- Recovery success rate
- Human intervention rate
- Automation coverage
- Learning effectiveness

